 "Newcastle", "Revenue_GBP": 10510.57}, {"MonthNum": 12, "MonthName": "December", "RegionName": "London South", "Revenue_GBP": 19848.44}, {"MonthNum": 12, "MonthName": "December", "RegionName": "Bristol", "Revenue_GBP": 11604.5}, {"MonthNum": 12, "MonthName": "December", "RegionName": "Cardiff", "Revenue_GBP": 10952.380000000001}, {"MonthNum": 12, "MonthName": "December", "RegionName": "Manchester", "Revenue_GBP": 16634.16}], "code": "SELECT CAST(f.MonthNum AS INTEGER) AS MonthNum, CASE CAST(f.MonthNum AS INTEGER) WHEN 1 THEN 'January' WHEN 2 THEN 'February' WHEN 3 THEN 'March' WHEN 4 THEN 'April' WHEN 5 THEN 'May' WHEN 6 THEN 'June' WHEN 7 THEN 'July' WHEN 8 THEN 'August' WHEN 9 THEN 'September' WHEN 10 THEN 'October' WHEN 11 THEN 'November' WHEN 12 THEN 'December' END AS MonthName, r.RegionName, SUM(f.TotalRevenue_GBP) AS Revenue_GBP FROM fact_financial_summary f JOIN dim_region r ON f.RegionID = r.RegionID WHERE f.Year = 2024 GROUP BY CAST(f.MonthNum AS INTEGER), MonthName, r.RegionName ORDER BY MonthNum", "attempts": 2, "insights": ["Edinburgh consistently leads revenue, peaking at \u00a319,051 in May \u2014 highest single region-month figure.", "Bristol and Cardiff are the lowest contributors each month, rarely exceeding \u00a310,500.", "Monthly total revenue grew from ~\u00a3119,938 in January to ~\u00a3140,542 in May, a ~17% increase.", "Manchester surged to \u00a317,629 in April, its strongest month, up 35% from January's \u00a312,322."], "recommendations": ["Investigate Edinburgh and Birmingham's growth drivers and replicate tactics in Bristol and Cardiff.", "Target January-to-February dip months with promotional campaigns to sustain early-year momentum.", "Set Q3 benchmarks using May's total as a baseline to track continued revenue growth trajectory."], "forecast": "Revenue shows a consistent upward trend from January through May across most regions, suggesting H2 totals could surpass H1 if current momentum holds. Edinburgh and Manchester's strong growth trajectories position them as key drivers for full-year performance."}}, {"id": "9n1qwEj3G6I", "owner": "marcus", "title": "Drill into \"Feb 2024\". Based on my previous question (Create a stacked bar chart of monthly revenue from January to December, with each bar split into 4 territo", "kind": "bar", "recipients": ["fo@houseofcolour.com"], "day_of_month": 1, "created": "2026-06-24T08:25:20.858741+00:00", "data": {"chart_type": "bar", "x": "StylistName", "y": "TotalRevenue_GBP", "series": null, "title": "Feb 2024 Revenue by Stylist", "explanation": "This bar chart drills into February 2024 and shows total revenue broken down by individual stylist (via their consultant linkage), revealing which stylists contributed most to that month's performance across all territory segments.", "columns": ["StylistName", "TotalRevenue_GBP"], "rows": [{"StylistName": "Tom Davis", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6611.81}, {"StylistName": "Liam Wilson", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6611.81}, {"StylistName": "Raj Miller", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6611.81}, {"StylistName": "Oliver Moore", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6611.81}, {"StylistName": "Claire Hughes", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6257.71}, {"StylistName": "Sarah Walsh", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6257.71}, {"StylistName": "Lisa Carter", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6257.71}, {"StylistName": "Anna Singh", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6257.71}, {"StylistName": "Daisy Evans", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6214.13}, {"StylistName": "Poppy Phillips", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6214.13}, {"StylistName": "Freya Parker", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 6214.13}, {"StylistName": "Rachel Johnson", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5765.13}, {"StylistName": "David Brown", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5765.13}, {"StylistName": "Mark Taylor", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5765.13}, {"StylistName": "James Smith", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5765.13}, {"StylistName": "Violet Howard", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5531.03}, {"StylistName": "Willow Ward", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5531.03}, {"StylistName": "Dylan James", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5299.23}, {"StylistName": "Ethan Watson", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5299.23}, {"StylistName": "Mason Brooks", "TotalRevenue_GBP": 5299.23}], "code": "SELECT s.StylistName, SUM(f.TotalRevenue_GBP) AS TotalRevenue_GBP FROM fact_financial_summary f JOIN dim_consultant c ON f.ConsultantID = c.ConsultantID JOIN dim_stylist s ON s.ConsultantID = c.ConsultantID WHERE f.Year = 2024 AND f.MonthNum = 2 GROUP BY s.StylistName ORDER BY TotalRevenue_GBP DESC LIMIT 20", "attempts": 2, "insights": ["Top 4 stylists (Tom Davis, Liam Wilson, Raj Miller, Oliver Moore) each earned identical \u00a36,611.81 in Feb 2024.", "Three distinct revenue tiers exist: \u00a36,611, \u00a36,257, \u00a36,214, \u00a35,765, \u00a35,531, and \u00a35,299.", "Bottom 3 stylists (Dylan James, Ethan Watson, Mason Brooks) at \u00a35,299 earn 20% less than the top tier.", "Several stylists share identical revenues, suggesting possible territory-based flat allocation rather than individual performance."], "recommendations": ["Investigate why multiple stylists share exact revenues \u2014 confirm data reflects real bookings, not aggregation artefacts.", "Support bottom-tier stylists (\u00a35,299) with targeted coaching to close the \u00a31,312 gap to top performers.", "Review whether territory size differences explain revenue tiers and rebalance territories if inequitable."], "forecast": ""}}, {"id": "-h45eK7TrgY", "owner": "marcus", "title": "Show me monthly revenue trend broken down by territory (Canada, Ireland, United Kingdom, United States) as a stacked bar chart for the full year.", "kind": "bar", "recipients": ["fo@houseofcolour.com"], "day_of_month": 1, "created": "2026-06-24T06:10:39.570653+00:00", "data": {"chart_type": "bar", "x": "YearMonth", "y": "Revenue_GBP", "title": "Monthly Revenue by Region (2024)", "explanation": "The schema covers UK-based regions only (e.g. London North, London South) \u2014 there is no data for Canada, Ireland, or the United States. The chart instead shows monthly revenue broken down by the available UK regions for 2024, which is the c